prayerTemplate:
PRAYER

In the light of the facts and circumstances stated above, the Applicant / Aggrieved Person most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Pass a PROTECTION ORDER under Section 18 of the PWDV Act, 2005 restraining the Respondent from committing any act of domestic violence, entering the place of employment of the Applicant, attempting to communicate with the Applicant, alienating any assets, or causing violence to her dependants;

b) Pass a RESIDENCE ORDER under Section 19 (i) restraining the Respondent from dispossessing the Applicant from the shared household at {shared_household_address}, (ii) directing the Respondent to remove himself from the shared household, and/or (iii) directing the Respondent to secure same level of alternate accommodation;

c) Pass a MONETARY RELIEF ORDER under Section 20 directing the Respondent to pay (i) maintenance of Rs. ____/- per month; (ii) medical expenses of Rs. ____; (iii) loss of earnings of Rs. ____; (iv) rent / mortgage of Rs. ____;

d) Pass a CUSTODY ORDER under Section 21 granting temporary custody of the minor child(ren) to the Applicant;

e) Pass a COMPENSATION ORDER under Section 22 directing the Respondent to pay Rs. {compensation_amount}/- as compensation for mental torture and emotional distress caused;

f) Pass an ex-parte interim order under Section 23(2) pending final disposal;

g) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

And for this act of kindness, the Applicant shall ever pray.
